# Documentation Rules

## Always keep docs current

- After any investigation milestone, reconstruction, or convention change: update the matching notes and `.cursor/rules`. Do not leave stale or contradictory documentation.
- Prefer editing existing files over creating duplicates. Search `docs/` and `investigations/` before writing a new file.
- What to document: target identity, authorization basis, Evidence IDs, limitations, unknowns, and things agents must NOT do.

## Doc location and naming

- Workspace how-to docs live in `docs/` as `SCREAMING_SNAKE.md` (`START_HERE.md`, `AUTHORIZATION.md`).
- Per-target notes live in `investigations/<slug>/` with the fixed names in `structure.mdc`.
- A new investigation must include: one-sentence purpose, artifact path, authorization, questions, and an evidence ledger.

## Cursor rules maintenance

- If a change affects patterns other agents need, update `.cursor/rules/` as well as prose docs.
- Cross-cutting concerns → `global-rules.mdc`. REA workflow → `rea.mdc`. Domain-specific → the matching rule file.
- New rule files must use the `.mdc` extension.
- Model names in `models.mdc` go stale every few months. Refresh against [cursor.com/docs/models](https://cursor.com/docs/models).

## Trigger: "update docs"

When the user says "update documentation", "update docs", "update the docs", or similar, run the **`update-docs` skill**. Don't ask which files to update — the skill finds them.
